## URL Examples

```text
overlay.html?twitch=ninja&theme=neon&anim=slide&pos=right&size=14&dur=25&max=20
overlay.html?yt_key=YOUR_KEY&yt_vid=VIDEO_ID&theme=cyber&anim=float
overlay.html?kick=trainwreck&avatar=https://example.com/logo.png&demo=0
overlay.html?demo=1&theme=mono&status=0
```

## OBS Steps

1. Host the files on GitHub Pages, Netlify, Vercel, or another static host.
2. Open `index.html` and generate the overlay URL.
3. Add a Browser Source in OBS.
4. Paste the URL.
5. Set a resolution that gives the chat room enough room to breathe.
6. Use the transparent CSS fallback if needed.

## Behavior Summary

- Twitch connects anonymously over IRC WebSocket.
- YouTube polls the live chat API using your API key.
- Kick subscribes to the channel chat WebSocket.
- Demo mode cycles through example messages so you can test the design without a live source.

## Notes

- The overlay is static and does not need a build step.
- Message cards expire automatically after the configured duration.
- The visible message count is capped so the overlay stays readable.
- Platform badges and event cards are generated from the payload when the platform exposes that data.
